dialect protocol
protocol stdio.pdf.diff
version 1
schema stdio.pdf.diff
start diff

# P2-FG3: `protocol::DiffCodec::encode_diff`/`decode_diff` for `stdio.pdf` (1.4)'s `PdfDiff` are
# hand-rolled (../../🦀️.rs's `DiffCodec` region) since ticket
# 26/08/23/END-TO-END-TESTING-REFACTOR gave this standard a real page tree and turned its diff into
# an index-keyed collection triple. The previous `#[derive(dsl::DslDiff)]` route wrapped the record
# in the FULL `.spk` document container (`🎒️pack/📐️format/🦀️.rs`) — a checksummed,
# chunk-table-indexed, optionally-deflate-compressed random-access FILE format, which is a great
# deal of machinery for a per-message diff frame and which this dialect can only model down to its
# 24-byte superblock before the rest becomes one opaque tail.
#
# The hand-rolled frame is the same one the sibling 1.7 standard's diff writes, and it is fully
# walkable at its own header: a fixed `format` byte (`store::pack_rt::OP_BINARY_FORMAT`), a `flags`
# byte whose bit 0 marks the `pages` lane's presence, and — when set — the page triple's own
# genuinely structured payload (three varint-counted lists; `modified` items carry a per-field
# presence-flagged `PdfPageDiff`, `added` items carry two little-endian `f64`s and a
# length-prefixed text).
#
# `chain payload bytes` past the 2-byte header is the honest boundary: the triple is a
# count-driven, recursively-encoded structure this dialect has no repeat-with-inner-dispatch
# primitive for. The Rust side stays genuinely structured and is round-trip tested independently
# (`diff_codec_text_binary_roundtrip_law`).
framing record
header fixed 2
field format u8
field flags u8
chain payload bytes
